   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In late 2013, CDC invested $20 million into CPCIF, the only infrastructure fund that is dedicated solely to the information and communications technology (ICT) sector in Africa.&#xa0; Our $20 million commitment contributes a total of $145 million to the fund&#x2019;s first close, supported mostly by DFIs.&#xa0; The fund reached its final close at $186.5 million with participation from Sango Capital (a private sector investor) and the Public Investment Corporation of South Africa.&#xa0;Our capital was used to develop communications infrastructure and related services and technologies across sub-Saharan Africa.</narrative>
   </description>
